    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, im seeing a CrashLoopBackOff on one of our microservices in GKE. i checked the logs but it's mostly just exiting with code 137. can u give me a checklist of what to look at to see if its a memory issue or maybe a readiness probe failing? i need to narrow this down fast.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "First, check the `Container-Manifest` in GKE to see if the liveness/readiness probe status is failing, as a non-HTTP port often returns exit code 137 if the container receives `SIGKILL`. You can verify this in the GKE console under the pod's detail tab. If you confirm this, check your deployment manifests and resource limits to see if the container is hitting its memory limits or receiving `OOMKilled` statuses. Finally, look at the recently unused pods, which could indicate memory pressure sharing across nodes and potentially causing this crash loop.",
      "source": "target",
