    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. i checked the pod details and it's definitely showing OOMKilled. the limits seem okay on paper but it keeps spiking. do u think it's a leak in the app itself or could it be something with how the node is managing the cgroup limits? any idea how to debug which specific process/thread is eating it all?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, it is likely a memory leak in the application itself, as sudden spikes indicating a gradual leak are common, but a zombie process or outlier thread can also cause this. Since you have the OOMKilled status, you can debug the specific source by examining `/var/lib/docker/containers/<container-id>/memory_usage.json` inside the container's file system to see which thread held the most memory. If that isn't accessible, attach a temporary container to the pod and run `pmap -x <pid>` or analyze `/proc/<pid>/smaps` while the process is still running to pinpoint the exact memory consumer.",
      "source": "target",
